7. Identity Tables Added to Database

Table Name
	

Purpose

AspNetUsers
	

Stores user accounts (email, password hash, etc.)

AspNetRoles
	

Stores role definitions (Admin, Customer, Vendor)

AspNetUserRoles
	

Maps users to their assigned roles

AspNetUserClaims
	

Stores additional user claims

AspNetUserLogins
	

Tracks external login providers

AspNetUserTokens
	

Stores user tokens (reset, 2FA, etc.)

AspNetRoleClaims
	

Stores claims associated with roles

 
8. Notes & Next Steps
Current Limitations

•       Login returns a plain 200 OK — no JWT token is issued yet.

•       Endpoints are currently unprotected — no [Authorize] attribute applied.

•       No refresh token or session management implemented.
Recommended Next Steps

•       Add JWT Bearer authentication and return a signed token on login.

•       Apply [Authorize(Roles = "Admin")] to protected endpoints.

•       Add a /api/auth/logout endpoint that clears the session/token.

•       Move RegisterDto and LoginDto into a dedicated Models/Dtos/ folder.

•       Add input validation attributes (e.g. [Required], [EmailAddress]) to DTOs.

•       Consider moving role seeding to a dedicated DataSeeder service class.

 